# Agent orientation

This repository uses the **AI-agent methodology** (plan → agree → implement; verify at the consumer-visible
contract; the human owns every external action). This file is read by every Copilot surface (CLI, VS Code,
cloud agent, code review) — keep it short: orientation and pointers only.

## Read first every session

1. If present, the machine-local identity card `data/changes/s3-sync/IDENTITY.md` (role: publisher or
   contributor — read it before writing anything shared).
2. Live snapshot: `data/changes/STATUS.md`. Danger zones: `data/changes/SHARP_EDGES.md`.
3. Scoped gates load automatically from `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md`.
4. Full pack (on demand): `data/changes/ai-agent-methodology/COPILOT_ADAPTATION.md`.

## Do not load by default

Per-ticket writeups, playbooks and long history under `data/changes/<id>/` — open on demand only.

## Output contract

Define here (one paragraph): what downstream consumers actually observe (API JSON, UI field, event,
artifact). Every bug is reproduced and verified against that surface.

## Human-only actions

`git push`, `gh pr create|merge|ready`, the CLI's `/pr create`, `/pr auto` and `/pr automerge`, releases and
deploys are **human-only**. A `preToolUse` hook (`.github/hooks/block-external-git.json`) denies the shell
forms; do not try to work around it. Prepare the branch and a handover note instead.
